<title>THAILAND: Thai central bank says reviews 2-tier baht system.</title>
<headline>Thai central bank says reviews 2-tier baht system.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Assistant central bank governor Siri Garnjarerndee said on Tuesday the Bank of Thailand is reviewing its two-tier baht system adopted since mid-May but he declined to say whether it would be scrapped soon.</p>
<p>Siri told reporters the baht's two-tier system -- designed to cut off offshore baht supply used by currency speculators to attack the baht -- and foreign exchange controls would benefit Thailand only in the short-term.</p>
</text>
